[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. Read by tenant and by the
way each report came in, its reports are three problems. The fix queued for #4471 fixes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known. Three problems, three tickets. The queued parser fix leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

### `parser`: dates read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so a
booking for 2 December comes out as 12 February. It reaches us by app, email and form, from every
tenant. This is the bug #4471 names, and the queued fix is for it.

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. A day-first tenant's people type what the hint
says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. The symptom is the same swap, but the bug is in
the form, not the parser. It comes only through the form, only from tenants on booking-v3. The
parser fix does not touch it: the hint has to print the tenant's order.

### `one-day-move`: dates shift by one day

These reports describe a date that moved by a single day, not a swapped day and month: Tuesday 12
May showed as Monday 11 May; the same meeting landed on Tuesday for a client in Lisbon and on Monday
for a client in Toronto. A day–month swap cannot do that. The desk read them as one-day moves
(`desk-notes.json`), and the #4471 table still counts them under `parser`, by tenant. The cause is
not known yet; a time-zone conversion is the first thing to check.

## Why it became one ticket

- We merge on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All three problems
  come in with the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so the subject cannot
  tell them apart. The cause depends on the tenant, its booking form and the channel, which
  `causes.ts` already knows and the [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows.
- Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser. That guess disagrees with the problem for
  the reports counted under the table.
- A month swap and a one-day move look alike in a subject line. Only the body tells them apart.

## What the desk does now

1. Keep #4471 for `parser` only. Merge a new report there only when its tenant writes the day first
   and it did not come through booking-v3's form.
2. Merge form reports from booking-v3 tenants into the `hint` ticket.
3. Read the body before merging. A date that moved by one day goes to the `one-day-move` ticket, and
   its id goes into `desk-notes.json`; this table moves it on the next build.
4. Replace decision 0001 with a new record that dedupes by cause, not by subject.

